# BUSY Bar Agent Status

When the Fulcrum Builds Pi is reachable, update its BUSY Bar with
`busybar_control.py` before and after appliance changes:

1. Before editing files, installing dependencies, deploying, committing, or
   pushing, run:
   `ssh -i ~/.ssh/xerogrid-signage signage@10.117.186.125 "sudo BUSYBAR_ADDRESS=10.0.4.20 /opt/digital-signage/venv/bin/python /opt/digital-signage/bin/busybar_control.py agent 'MAKING CHANGES'"`
2. After all changes and verification finish, or when waiting on the user,
   show idle status:
   `ssh -i ~/.ssh/xerogrid-signage signage@10.117.186.125 "BUSYBAR_ADDRESS=10.0.4.20 /opt/digital-signage/venv/bin/python /opt/digital-signage/bin/busybar_control.py sleeping"`
3. Restore the booth preset only when that is the intended display:
   `ssh -i ~/.ssh/xerogrid-signage signage@10.117.186.125 "BUSYBAR_ADDRESS=10.0.4.20 /opt/digital-signage/venv/bin/python /opt/digital-signage/bin/busybar_control.py signage"`

Use a short custom detail when helpful (`DEPLOY SIGNAGE`, `RESTART KIOSK`).
If the Pi, private key, or local network is unavailable, continue without
blocking and report that the indicator could not be updated.
